title: 2025 / 07 / 15 / प्रेषयामास

The phrase "sent him away" in Sanskrit may be expressed in several elegant ways depending on context, but the most straightforward rendering is:

<<<
"तम् प्रेषयामास।" — He sent him.
<<<

To emphasize "away" — in the sense of dismissal or sending to a distant place, we can use appropriate upasargas (prefixes) with the verbs:

<<<
 √प्रेष् / √दिश् / √स्था / √गम्, etc.
<<<

🔹 Suitable Translations:

तम् दूरं प्रेषयामास।
He sent him far away.

तम् विसृज्य प्रस्थापयामास।
:Having dismissed him, he sent him away (on a journey).

तम् निर्गमयामास।
He caused him to depart.
(Here, नि + √गम्, causative form = "to send out".)
तम् विसर्जयामास।

He discharged/released/sent him away.
(Used often when the departure is formal or dismissive.)